# .gitattributes — Star Stuff
#
# Two things only, and both exist because this repo gained a second contributor on
# 2026-09-14. Before that there was one checkout, so there were no merges and no
# second machine to disagree with the first.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. NEVER NORMALISE LINE ENDINGS. This is not a style preference.
#
# Four generators here verify their output by BYTE-COMPARING what they would write
# today against what is committed (`--check` on build-derived, build-csp,
# build-changelog, build-markdown). Git's `text=auto` rewrites line endings on
# checkout, per platform — so a file written on one machine and checked out on
# another could differ by exactly the bytes those gates compare, and every one of
# them would report STALE on a tree nobody had touched. Store and check out as-is.
* -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. `search-index.json` IS 6.1 MB ON ONE LINE, and git must not try to merge it.
#
# It is generated by `tools/build-search-index.mjs` from a headless render of all
# 200-odd pages, and it is minified to a single line. A textual three-way merge of
# one 6 MB line is not a merge: git either produces a conflict nobody can read or,
# worse, splices two JSON documents into one that parses and is wrong — a search
# index that silently points readers at passages that moved.
#
# `-merge` makes git refuse and leave the conflict standing; `-diff` stops it
# rendering a six-megabyte line as a diff. The resolution is never by hand:
#
#     git checkout --ours search-index.json   # either side; both are about to be replaced
#     node tools/check-derived.mjs --write    # regenerates all five, in dependency order
#     git add search-index.json
#
# The same rule holds for every other derived file (whats-new.html, feed.xml,
# llms.txt, changelog.html, _headers, the 57 .md siblings) even though those merge
# legibly and are left alone here: a derived file is a copy, and the way to resolve
# a disagreement between two copies is to ask the thing they are copies OF.
search-index.json -merge -diff linguist-generated=true
